# Line endings are pinned rather than left to each machine's git config.
#
# CI runs this repository on ubuntu and on windows in the same commit, and the
# PowerShell job reads the same files as the Python job. LF everywhere is the
# setting that makes both true: Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads LF without
# complaint, and a shell script or a TOML file that arrives with CRLF on Linux
# fails in ways that read as a bug in the file rather than in the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one place the ending is part of the format rather than a preference.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf

# Not text. Nothing here should be line-ending-converted or diffed as prose.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.iso binary
